      "content": "thanks. looking at it closer, i'm wondering if there's even a real \"debate\" left if we're talking about \"certainty\" of long-term risk vs just some \"potential\" economic issues. i mean, isn't the economic stuff just a temporary hurdle that can be managed with policy, whereas the climate stuff is literally an existential threat? how do you even weigh those two things if one is a certainty and the other is just a cost?",
